      "text": "A smooth evolutionary transformation on a clean white studio background.\n\nThe animation begins with @1, a soft sponge-like multicellular organism floating gently in mid-air. The organism is centered in frame with generous white space around it. It drifts slowly forward toward the camera.\n\nAs the organism moves forward, the body begins evolving.\n\nThe porous organic structure gradually becomes more structured and symmetrical. The soft tissue slowly compresses and reorganizes into layered biological plates.\n\nSegments begin forming along the length of the body as the organism transitions into an early arthropod body plan.\n\nA hard exoskeleton slowly develops, replacing the soft porous surface. The body becomes flatter and more segmented, forming distinct ridged plates along the back.\n\nSmall jointed appendages begin to appear beneath the body, and the head structure becomes more defined.\n\nCompound eyes slowly form on either side of the head as the shell hardens and the segmentation becomes fully articulated.\n\nBy the end of the transformation the organism has evolved into @2, a fully formed trilobite floating slightly above the white studio surface.\n\nThe creature now crawls slowly forward with subtle movement of its segmented body and small legs.\n\nThe camera remains locked in a frontal view with consistent scale and framing throughout the transformation.\n\nLighting remains soft and neutral to match the reference images.\n\nThe morph should feel organic and biological, with tissues restructuring, plates forming, and segmentation emerging naturally over time.",
